    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0369" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1533.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commissioner Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date><hi rendition="#italic">; received October 1,
                            1914.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Presidential candidates will be Jiménez, Vásquez, Velásquez and Vidal. General
                    pacification is advancing. Commission constantly watchful. Apparently good
                    feeling prevails at present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
